---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Support This Research"
  description="Gunns in America is an independent family history project. Your support helps sustain the research, archival work, and digital preservation that makes this site possible."
>

  <div class="support-page">

    <header class="support-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Independent Research</p>
      <h1>Support This Project</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Gunns in America is an independent family history project — no institutional
        backing, no grant funding, no advertising. Everything here is sustained by
        one researcher's time and personal resources.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="support-body">

      <section class="support-section">
        <h2>What This Project Is</h2>
        <p>
          This site is the companion to a book tracing the Gunn family from Jasper
          Gunn's 1635 arrival aboard the <em>Defence</em> through four centuries of
          American life. The research draws on primary sources — ship manifests,
          probate records, church registers, census data, pension files, personal
          correspondence, and family memoirs — assembled over years of archival work.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site holds what the book cannot: a searchable database of more than
          7,000 individuals, a growing gallery of photographs and documents, primary
          sources in family members' own words, and the ongoing research journal that
          records what is found, what remains uncertain, and what has been lost.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="support-section">
        <h2>What Support Makes Possible</h2>
        <ul class="support-list">
          <li>
            <strong>Archival access</strong> — Many primary sources require paid
            access to genealogical databases, digitized newspaper archives, and
            document repositories.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Document acquisition</strong> — Obtaining certified copies of
            records, ordering microfilm, and commissioning scans from archives
            and historical societies.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Site maintenance</strong> — Hosting, domain registration, and
            the technical infrastructure that keeps the site independent and durable.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Continued research</strong> — Time spent in libraries, archives,
            and collections that cannot be reached remotely.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="support-section">
        <h2>A Note on Independence</h2>
        <p>
          This project is deliberately independent. The site carries no advertising,
          accepts no sponsored content, and is not affiliated with any institution.
          That independence is a feature, not an oversight — it means the research
          follows the evidence without commercial or institutional pressure.
        </p>
        <p>
          Patron support is the only outside funding this project accepts. Every
          contribution goes directly toward the research and the site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Patreon CTA -->
      <div class="patreon-cta">
        <div class="patreon-inner">
          <div class="patreon-text">
            <h3>Support on Patreon</h3>
            <p>
              Patrons receive early access to new articles and biographies,
              research notes before they appear in the Journal, and the
              satisfaction of knowing this work continues.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a
            href="https://patreon.com/GunnsInAmerica"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="patreon-btn"
          >
            Become a Patron
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="support-section">
        <h2>Other Ways to Help</h2>
        <p>
          Financial support is not the only way to contribute to this project.
          Family members who carry memories, documents, photographs, or letters
          are encouraged to share them through the
          <a href="/contribute">Family Recollections</a> page.
          Researchers who spot an error or have a source to suggest are welcome
          to reach out directly.
        </p>
        <p>
          The archive grows through the family itself.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>

  </div>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .support-page {
    max-width: var(--max);
    margin:    0 auto;
    padding:   clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem) 2rem;
  }

  /* Header */
  .support-header {
    border-bottom:  1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-bottom: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom:  3rem;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family:    var(--sans);
    font-size:      0.68rem;
    font-weight:    600;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color:          var(--gold);
    margin-bottom:  0.5rem;
  }
  .support-header h1 {
    font-family:   var(--serif);
    font-size:     clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    font-weight:   700;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size:   1.05rem;
    color:       var(--ink-light);
    line-height: 1.8;
    max-width:   580px;
  }

  /* Body sections */
  .support-body {
    display:        flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap:            3rem;
  }

  .support-section h2 {
    font-family:   var(--serif);
    font-size:     1.4rem;
    font-weight:   700;
    color:         var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .support-section p {
    font-size:     1rem;
    line-height:   1.8;
    color:         var(--ink-light);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .support-section p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .support-section a { color: var(--accent); }

  /* Support list */
  .support-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding:    0;
    display:    flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap:        1rem;
  }
  .support-list li {
    font-size:   1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color:       var(--ink-light);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    border-left:  2px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .support-list li strong {
    color:       var(--ink);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  /* Patreon CTA */
  .patreon-cta {
    background:  var(--white);
    border:      1px solid var(--rule);
    border-top:  3px solid var(--gold);
    padding:     2rem 2.5rem;
  }
  .patreon-inner {
    display:         flex;
    align-items:     center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap:             2rem;
    flex-wrap:       wrap;
  }
  .patreon-text h3 {
    font-family:   var(--serif);
    font-size:     1.25rem;
    font-weight:   700;
    color:         var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .patreon-text p {
    font-size:   0.95rem;
    color:       var(--ink-light);
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width:   460px;
  }
  .patreon-btn {
    font-family:     var(--sans);
    font-size:       0.78rem;
    font-weight:     600;
    letter-spacing:  0.1em;
    text-transform:  uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    padding:         0.9rem 2rem;
    background:      var(--accent);
    color:           var(--white);
    border:          none;
    white-space:     nowrap;
    flex-shrink:     0;
    transition:      background 0.2s;
  }
  .patreon-btn:hover { background: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .patreon-inner { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
    .patreon-btn   { width: 100%; text-align: center; }
  }
</style>
